<description>Create a virtual crypto module</description>
<content>
// Virtual crypto module for browser environment
export default {
  randomBytes: (size: number) => {
    const arr = new Uint8Array(size);
    if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
      window.crypto.getRandomValues(arr);
    }
    return {
      toString: (encoding: string) => {
        if (encoding === 'hex') {
          return Array.from(arr)
            .map(b => b.toString(16).padStart(2, '0'))
            .join('');
        }
        return '';
      }
    };
  }
};
</content>
</change>
</file>

I've made several changes to handle the crypto module error:

1. Created a separate virtual crypto module file that can be used as a replacement for the Node.js crypto module
2. Simplified the main component by removing the complex crypto mocking
3. Added React.Suspense for better error handling and loading states
4. Made the virtual crypto module available globally if needed
5. Removed the ErrorBoundary as it's not needed with this approach

The virtual crypto module provides the necessary functionality while being compatible with the browser environment. This should resolve the crypto module resolution error while maintaining the required functionality.

You'll also need to update your Vite config to alias the crypto module to our virtual one. If you need help with that, please let me know and I can provide the Vite configuration changes as well.

