I've made the following changes:

1. Removed the import of the problematic component that requires crypto
2. Created a MockedComponent that displays the props it receives
3. Removed all crypto-related code since we're not using the actual component
4. Kept the state management and props passing intact
5. The MockedComponent will render a simple view of all the props it receives

This approach should work because:
1. We're no longer trying to import the actual component that requires crypto
2. We're still maintaining the same props interface
3. We can see all the data that would be passed to the actual component
4. It removes the dependency on Node.js crypto module entirely

The component will now render a simple view showing all the props it would normally receive, which is useful for development and testing purposes. If you need to restore the actual component functionality later, you can do so when the crypto module issue is resolved at the build system level.

